## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of basic network security controls in Azure and practical rollout/rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Private Link and Private Endpoints
- Storage Account network rules (default deny)
- Azure Policy enforcement
- Rollback and test strategies

## Code Example
```bicep
param storageAccountName string
param vnetSubnetId string
resource pe 'Microsoft.Network/privateEndpoints@2020-11-01' = {
  name: '${storageAccountName}-pe'
  location: resourceGroup().location
  properties: {
    subnet: { id: vnetSubnetId }
    privateLinkServiceConnections: [
      {
        name: 'storageBlob'
        properties: {
          privateLinkServiceId: '/subscriptions/.../resourceGroups/.../providers/Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/${storageAccountName}'
          groupIds: [ 'blob' ]
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        { "field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts" },
        { "not": { "field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/privateEndpointConnections", "exists": true } }
        }
      ]
    },
    "then": { "effect": "deny" }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify the guardrail in CI/CD pipelines?
- How would you extend to multi-region deployments and private DNS considerations?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement defense-in-depth for cross-tenant OAuth security and a robust rollback.

## Key Concepts
- OAuth2/OIDC, Managed Identities, Conditional Access, PIM
- Private Endpoints, VNet integration, RBAC scoping
- Defender for Cloud, UEBA, alerting
- Secrets rotation and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal token validation sketch for a Node.js API
const express = require('express');
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authorize(requiredScope) {
  return (req, res, next) => {
    const token = req.headers.authorization?.split(' ')[1];
    if (!token) return res.sendStatus(401);
    const decoded = jwt.decode(token, { complete: true });
    if (!decoded || !decoded.payload.scp?.includes(requiredScope)) return res.sendStatus(403);
    next();
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test token leakage incidents and validate rollback effectiveness?
- What telemetry and dashboards would you provision to detect anomaly token usage?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical incident response design, Azure Key Vault integrations, and rollback discipline using beginner-friendly tooling.

## Key Concepts
- Incident response workflow
- Azure Key Vault secret rotation
- Managed Identities for AAD auth
- Event Grid / Gateways for triggering automation
- Rollback strategy with last-known-good secret

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-rotate-secret workflow (illustrative)
async function rotateSecret(vault, name) {
  const newValue = generateSecret();
  await vault.setSecret({ name, value: newValue });
  // notify apps to refresh
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
